# The dead watch of the Tsolenka tower: Sergeant Dorin Valcu, his watchman, and the gate winch
# (docs/regions/berez.md §3.3).

~ sergeant
if flag.tsolenka_watch_fate == "passed"
-> passed_again
endif
if not flag.tsolenka_watch_met
set tsolenka_watch_met
quest the_tsolenka_gate reached
Narrator: Five soldiers in old mail stand at their posts around the guardroom, grey as the stone behind them and a little blurred at the edges, like breath on a cold window. One of them steps out into the middle of the floor. He has sergeant's knots on his shoulder and no colour in him anywhere.
tsolenka_sergeant: Halt. Watchword.
else
tsolenka_sergeant: Halt. Watchword.
Narrator: He says it exactly the same way as last time. You suspect he has said it exactly the same way for centuries.
endif
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel says discipline is carrying on after the reason's gone. I don't think he meant this.
if guest:kasimir_velikov
interject guest:kasimir_velikov: My sister came this way. If they stopped her, they'll remember. If they didn't, they let her through to that place, and I don't know which I'd rather hear.
endif
-> watch_menu

~ watch_menu
* [if flag.tsolenka_watchword_known] Cold hearth, shut door. -> watchword
* [if not flag.tsolenka_lie_tried] [Deception DC 15] We're the relief. Your watch is over. -> relief | relief_fail
* [if not flag.tsolenka_release_tried] [Persuasion DC 15] Sergeant, the crown that gave you your orders is gone, and so are you. -> release | release_fail
* [if not flag.tsolenka_release_tried] [Religion DC 13] Let us say the words for your lads, and stand the watch while they rest. -> release | release_fail
* [Cleric] (Offer the rites of the dead.) -> release
* What are you guarding? -> guarding
* [if treasure_at:tsolenka_pass_guard_tower] What's in the captain's room? -> captains_room
* Stand aside, sergeant, or be made to. -> fight
* We'll go. -> leave

~ guarding
tsolenka_sergeant: The road. Nothing comes down the mountain. Nobody goes up it. Those are the orders. I didn't write them; I keep them.
tsolenka_sergeant: Two of the lads went up once, on their own, at night. They came back talking about voices in the amber that knew their names. We sent them down to the valley. I don't know what became of them.
interject tag:curious: What's up there, sergeant?
tsolenka_sergeant: Not my business, traveller. My business is the gate.
-> watch_menu

~ captains_room
tsolenka_sergeant: Captain's things. Off limits. And something that came up the road a while back in a dead man's pack, that the captain locked away and wouldn't talk about. You'll keep out of there, if you know what's good.
-> watch_menu

~ watchword
set tsolenka_watch_fate = "passed"
quest the_tsolenka_gate watch_passed
Narrator: The sergeant's eyes, which are not really there, rest on you for a long moment.
tsolenka_sergeant: Cold hearth, shut door. That's the word. Pass, then. Winch is through there, in the gatehouse. Mind the chain; it bites. Log it when you're done.
interject tag:blunt: Log it where?
tsolenka_sergeant: Anywhere. Nobody reads it.
-> END

~ relief
set tsolenka_lie_tried
set tsolenka_watch_fate = "passed"
quest the_tsolenka_gate watch_passed
tsolenka_sergeant: Relief. Relief. About time, I'd say, if I had the breath to say it with.
Narrator: He turns to his men and says something you don't catch. They stand easier. One of them, very quietly, sits down for the first time in a very long time.
tsolenka_sergeant: Winch is in the gatehouse. The watch is yours.
-> END

~ relief_fail
set tsolenka_lie_tried
tsolenka_sergeant [angry]: Relief comes with the watchword and a written order, and you've neither. Liars on the mountain road. That's the oldest trick there is.
Narrator: Five grey hands go to five grey sword hilts, and stay there, waiting for a reason.
-> watch_menu

~ release
set tsolenka_watch_released
set tsolenka_watch_fate = "released"
quest the_tsolenka_gate watch_passed
Narrator: The sergeant listens. His men listen. When it's done, nobody moves for a while.
tsolenka_sergeant: Gone. All of it. The crown, the valley we kept it for. And us.
tsolenka_sergeant: Well. Somebody might have said. Lads: stand down.
Narrator: They go one at a time, the youngest first, like candles at the end of a long night. The sergeant goes last. He looks at the gate, and then at you, and nods once, as if signing something over.
interject class:cleric: Rest. You kept it long enough.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2: You let the dead watch of Tsolenka stand down
-> END

~ release_fail
set tsolenka_release_tried
tsolenka_sergeant: Nice words. I've heard nice words before, at this gate, from people who wanted to go up the road. Watchword, traveller.
-> watch_menu

~ fight
set tsolenka_watch_fate = "fought"
tsolenka_sergeant: Then you'll be made to, and we'll log it. Watch! To me!
approve godrick_pendlebrook -1 liriel_dawnsong -1: You fought your way through the dead watch of Tsolenka
combat tsolenka_watch

~ leave
tsolenka_sergeant: Go back down. Go home. That's the best advice this tower has.
-> END

~ passed_again
tsolenka_sergeant: Travellers. You've passed. The winch is in the gatehouse. Nothing came down. Nobody went up. Well, you did. I've logged it.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The watchman at his post

~ watchman
Narrator: The grey soldier at his post doesn't look at you. His eyes are on the door to the road, exactly where they have been for centuries.
tsolenka_watchman: Talk to the sergeant.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The gate winch (prop in the gatehouse)

~ winch
if flag.tsolenka_gate_open
Narrator: The chain is run out to its last link and wedged with a peg. Through the murder holes you can see the portcullis standing up in its slot, and the road beyond it climbing into the cloud.
-> END
endif
if not flag.tsolenka_watch_released and not flag.tsolenka_watch_fought and flag.tsolenka_watch_fate != "passed"
Narrator: A grey hand closes over the crank before yours can. It is cold the way a well is cold.
tsolenka_sergeant: Not without the watchword, traveller.
-> END
endif
Narrator: A drum of black chain as tall as a man, a crank as long as a spear, and a ratchet that has been oiled by nobody for a very long time.
* Haul on the winch. -> winch_up
* Leave it. -> END

~ winch_up
set tsolenka_gate_open
quest the_tsolenka_gate open
Narrator: It takes all of you. The ratchet screams, then clicks, then clicks, and somewhere below the floor the portcullis lifts out of a groove it has worn into the road.
if flag.tsolenka_watch_fate == "passed"
tsolenka_sergeant: Gate up. Logged. May whatever you're going to find be worse at waiting than we were.
endif
if guest:kasimir_velikov
interject guest:kasimir_velikov: The road's open. She walked this. I can feel it.
endif
-> END
